		{"id":"259887ca8a12cb1d","type":"text","text":"General \nVisuals: An imposing figure with a banner, clad in golden armor. \n\"To carry more of the King's blood than any man, and to be humble before your lessers. This is what makes a General.\" \nCHAMPION UNIT \n2 MP to summon. \n9 LP Abilities: Align: Free. Choose an ally. All allies that share at least one subtype with the target will be bolstered 0/+1 on turn. \nUpgrade paths: \n1. Adds an ability Inspire: 5 LP. Choose an ally. Bolster it +[level * 2]/+[level].\n\n2. Adds an ability Fortification: 3 LP. Choose an ally. Grant it [level] Armor.,\n\n3. Improves Align. Now it grants Unity: +[level / 2]/+[level/ 2] instead.","x":820,"y":-200,"width":597,"height":389},
		{"id":"563751628e2de579","type":"text","text":"The King's Men serve the Throne with their lives. They are all nobles, possessing of the King's blood. This blood, by its very nature, compels them to gather in Ashk'lan in time of summons. The highest-ranking King's Men conceal their faces under golden masks, showing that they are nothing without service.\nTheir speaking style is generally haughty and hot-blooded.","x":-620,"y":560,"width":637,"height":145},
		{"id":"f790caaf0d956627","x":101,"y":545,"width":719,"height":176,"type":"text","text":"Askelan has its own set of gods, built up by the King's men, who are not the purview of the priestly class. In this pantheon, the King rules supreme, and his ancestors' spirits each is given their own domain. Then there are the Ur-Tekton and Dreige, the characters of the myth of the City's founding. Below that are heroes brought to divinity. From there, soldiers and ministers, bureaucrats and servants are all considered minor divinity in accordance with their rank."}
